    "# 03-Decision-Tree-Iris\n",
    "\n",
    "## Classification des Fleurs Iris avec Arbres de Décision\n",
    "\n",
    "Un classique du machine learning: classification multi-classes avec l'algorithme Decision Tree sur le dataset Iris.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 📋 Table des Matières\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Introduction\n",
    "2. Setup et Imports\n",
    "3. Chargement des Données\n",
    "4. Exploration\n",
    "5. Arbre de Décision\n",
    "6. Évaluation\n",
    "7. Visualisation de l'Arbre\n",
    "8. Tuning des Hyperparamètres\n",
    "9. Conclusion\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Introduction\n",
    "\n",
    "L'**arbre de décision** est un algorithme de classification et de régression qui utilise une structure arborescente pour prendre des décisions basées sur les caractéristiques des données.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Concepts clés:\n",
    "- **Nœuds de décision**: Questions sur les caractéristiques\n",
    "- **Nœuds feuilles**: Prédictions finales\n",
    "- **Gini Impurity**: Mesure de l'hétérogénéité d'un nœud\n",
    "- **Entropie**: Mesure de l'incertitude\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Bibliothèques chargées!\n",
      "Scikit-learn: 1.6.1\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from sklearn.datasets import load_iris\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split, GridSearchCV, cross_val_score\n",
    "from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeClassifier, plot_tree, export_text\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import (accuracy_score, precision_score, recall_score,\n",
    "                             f1_score, classification_report, confusion_matrix)\n",
    "from sklearn import tree\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.style.use('seaborn-v0_8-whitegrid')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Bibliothèques chargées!\")\n",
    "print(f\"Scikit-learn: {sklearn.__version__}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "DATASET IRIS\n",
      "============\n",
      "150 échantillons, 4 caractéristiques, 3 classes\n",
      "\n",
      "Classes:\n",
      "  0: Setosa (50)\n",
      "  1: Versicolor (50)\n",
      "  2: Virginica (50)\n",
      "\n",
      "Caractéristiques:\n",
      "  sepal_length: Longueur du sépale (cm)\n",
      "  sepal_width: Largeur du sépale (cm)\n",
      "  petal_length: Longueur du pétale (cm)\n",
      "  petal_width: Largeur du pétale (cm)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Chargement du dataset Iris\n",
    "iris = load_iris()\n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame(iris.data, columns=iris.feature_names)\n",
    "df['species'] = iris.target\n",
    "df['species_name'] = df['species'].map({0: 'setosa', 1: 'versicolor', 2: 'virginica'})\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 60)\n",
    "DATASET IRIS\n",
    "============\")\n",
    "print(f\"{len(df)} échantillons, {len(iris.feature_names)} caractéristiques, {len(iris.target_names)} classes\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nClasses:\")\n",
    "for i, name in enumerate(iris.target_names):\n",
    "    count = (df['species'] == i).sum()\n",
    "print(f\"  {i}: {name.capitalize()} ({count})\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nCaractéristiques:\")\n",
    "names_fr = {\n",
    "    'sepal length (cm)': 'Longueur du sépale (cm)',\n",
    "    'sepal width (cm)': 'Largeur du sépale (cm)',\n",
    "    'petal length (cm)': 'Longueur du pétale (cm)',\n",
    "    'petal width (cm)': 'Largeur du pétale (cm)'\n",
    "}\n",
    "for en, fr in names_fr.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"  {en}: {fr}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
